Algorithm

1. Start the program.

2. Read the number of vertices and the adjacency matrix.

3. Select the source vertex.

4. Initialize all distances to infinity and set the source distance to zero.

5. Apply Dijkstra's algorithm to calculate shortest distances.

6. Display the shortest distances from the selected source.

7. Enter a destination vertex and display its complete shortest path.

8. Enter an edge and its new weight.

9. Update the edge weight in the graph.

10. Run Dijkstra's algorithm again and display the updated shortest distances. 11. Stop the program.
